}

// The classic salon-book client-relationship marks, snapshotted per booking
// (K5, decision D1). Two axes: request-vs-discovery (BookingSource — a
// server-validated trust boundary) × new-vs-return (the pair's established
// booking history, same count the discovery fee uses). RNR is the Tovis-specific
// fourth cell: a returning client who rebooked via discovery without asking for
// this pro by name. SNAPSHOTTED once at create by the write boundary — never
// derived at read time, or a client's third booking would retroactively rewrite
// their first booking's label and the historical NR count (the number that says
// whether marketing works) would silently drift. See lib/booking/relationshipLabel.ts.
enum ClientRelationshipLabel {
  UNKNOWN // imported / pro-created / legacy rows — never guessed (BookingSource defaults to DISCOVERY, which was never a real signal for these)
  NR // new request: first booking together, client sought out THIS pro
  NNR // new non-request: first booking together, arrived via discovery
  RR // returning request: repeat client who sought out this pro (incl. aftercare rebooks)
  RNR // returning non-request: repeat client who arrived via discovery again
}

