enum ClientActionTokenKind {
  CONSULTATION_ACTION
  AFTERCARE_ACCESS
  // K10-B: unauthenticated deposit-payment link for a pro-created booking whose
  // client is often UNCLAIMED (ClientProfile.userId null) and so can never pass
  // requireClient() on the authed deposit route.
  DEPOSIT_PAYMENT
  // K12: the confirm/cancel/reschedule action link carried by appointment
  // reminders (/client/appointment/<token>). Not single-use — the client may
  // confirm and later come back to cancel or reschedule from the same message;
  // the token expires at the appointment start instead.
  APPOINTMENT_CONFIRMATION
  // K15: the consent-signature link (/client/consent/<token>). Pins the exact
  // ConsentFormVersion the client is shown at MINT time — publishing a new
  // version between the send and the signature must not change which words the
  // record attests to.
  //
  // NOT single-use, on the DEPOSIT_PAYMENT reasoning: completion is enforced by
  // the STATE, not by burning the token — here the unique
  // ClientConsentRecord.signatureTokenId, which makes a second signature
  // impossible at the database. Burning it instead would answer a client who
  // reopens the link to re-read what they agreed to with "invalid or expired",
  // when the truth is "you signed this, here it is".
  CONSENT_SIGNATURE
}

